# StegoRSA — Cryptoghraphy
Difficulty: easy
Tools: exiftool, Cyberchef, openssl

What I was given: An encrypted flag file and an image
What worked: Finding hidden message in the image and using it to decrypt the flag
Steps: 
  1. Download the files
  2. Open an online Exiftool
  3. Insert the image into the exiftool and copy the file comment in the meta data section
  4. Paste the file comment into CyberChef and convert it from HEX
  5. Copy the decoded RSA key to a file
  6. use openssl to decrypt the encrypted file using the RSA key (openssl pkeyutl -decrypt -inkey RSAkey.pem -in flag.enc -out flag.txt)
Things I learned: 
  1. Hidden data can be hid inside "innocent" looking file
  2. How to use openssl to decrypt file and messages
